    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW21jZfxe5AmskoMP3AYBnVbr)_\n\nBefore: the graphical splash (`sp-splash.el`, the screen with Agenda / Config / Mail / Notes / Projects) showed `lambda-logo-white.png` or `-black.png` above the title. `lambda-splash.txt` was only used by the terminal splash.\n\nAfter: the splash draws `libraries/lambda-splash.txt` behind the menu, in both dark and light themes, a little left of centre. The art only fills blank cells, so the title and buttons stay on top. The new face `sp-splash-art-face` is dim grey on a dark background and pale grey on a light one, so it follows the theme.\n\nPosition: `sp-splash-art-x-offset` (default -12 columns) and `sp-splash-art-y-offset` (default 0), measured from the art centred on the menu. In the splash, `S-<arrow>` nudges the art (steps set by `sp-splash-art-x-step` / `-y-step`), `0` resets it and `s` shows and copies the `setq` form for the current offsets. Nudges last until Emacs exits. Set `sp-splash-art-file` to nil to get the PNG logo back.\n\nAlso: the literate doc `docs/tangles/tooling/sp-splash.org` has a new \"Lambda art\" section (its blocks tangle to exactly the new `.el`, checked by script), and `CHANGELOG.org` has an entry.\n\n**Not tested:** the container has no Emacs, so nothing was run or byte-compiled. Please load the module and run `M-x sp-splash-screen`. Things to check: the art lines up behind the menu, the grey is visible but quiet on your themes, `S-<arrow>` works in your terminal/GUI, and the layout looks right in a small window.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01T2BcMQ3qdNUiW5oZRLQRsG)_",
